Ticket **#4471** was marked known as one parser bug. The merge put **two** causes in
the same ticket. Subject-line dedupe never asked which cause a report had.

## What is in #4471

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## The split

- **`parser`** — the shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants
  (booking-v2, and booking-v3 when the channel is not the form) get the month and day
  flipped. This is the cause #4471 was opened for.
- **`hint`** — on booking-v3 the form prints `MM/DD/YYYY`. Day-first people type what
  the hint says; the form then reads the value the tenant's way. That is a different
  bug. It has no ticket of its own.

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 stays the parser ticket. Open a separate ticket for `hint`. Do not keep merging
`hint` reports into #4471.
</Callout>

